{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwRmr9piizjsPMygWT22","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. I haven't opened the dashboard or checked that the rule's query matches any documents.\n\n**Data:** The logs data view (`timestamp` is the time field) holds web requests. The fields I used:\n- `response`: the status code, stored as a string, so I match it through `response.keyword`.\n- `bytes`\n- `extension`\n- `geo.src`\n- `clientip`\n- `agent`\n- `machine.os`\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-599ed815 Web logs overview\" has five panels and a default range of the last 7 days:\n- Total requests\n- Requests over time\n- Responses by status code\n- Average bytes by extension\n- Top source countries\n\nYou can open it at http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-599ed815-web-logs-overview-b782f0b65c2a.\n\n**Rule:** \"EFF-599ed815 5xx spike\" is an Elasticsearch query rule.\n- It runs every minute and looks at the last 5 minutes of `kibana_sample_data_logs`.\n- It fires when the number of documents with `response.keyword` matching `5[0-9][0-9]` is above 10.\n- I created it without any actions, so it will raise alerts in Kibana but won't notify anyone."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":163,"cache_read_input_tokens":20489,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":163},"output_tokens":430,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4eb1cb7-866c-5bbf-8d81-a8d5acd83be3","uuid":"c6f0a870-e5a6-4c62-ba18-e0340e3227c3","timestamp":"2026-10-12T00:52:24.980Z","request_id":"req_011CfwRmqxuUQv3WNiFw3M1g"}
